    {
      "id": "apply-change",
      "description": "transition.rs apply_change: one schema change applied to a working copy, and the line that describes it. Every Define is define-or-replace (DefineObject keeps the fields and constraints of an object type it relabels); changing an object type that does not exist, removing something that does not exist, and defining a built-in role (public, owner) are refused with the problem. define-trigger, define-automation and define-operation are define-or-replace; removing a trigger, an automation, an operation or a unique constraint that does not exist is refused, and an automation is not removed while a trigger names it (D-6539). A table left empty is none, so the schema hashes as one that never held it. define-setting and define-capability are define-or-replace, and removing a setting or a capability that is not held is refused, a table left empty being none (settings.rs and capabilities.rs apply_define and apply_remove). The ledger declarations are applied here (ledger.rs apply_change): declaring a unit, a pool or a limit again replaces it (a limit of the same unit, or of the same account: unit, owner and scope) and the limits are kept in order; removing one that is not declared is refused (no ledger unit <id>, no ledger pool <id>, no such limit of ledger unit <id>); a table left empty is none. Whether an account still names a unit or a pool is checked by ledger-removal-check, which can see the accounts. A separation of duties is defined or replaced and removed here (duties.rs apply): the id of a platform separation is neither declared again nor removed, removing one that is not declared is refused, and a table left empty is none. Every other change, which is one of the declarations of an object type, the removal of an object type or a role, a template, a token or the ownership record of a product, is applied by apply-meta-change (D-7340, D-7341); every schema built here carries the tables of settings and capabilities, the ledger declarations and the tables of templates, tokens and products on.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        },
        {
          "name": "change",
          "type": "schema-change"
        }
      ],
