    {
      "id": "intent-decision",
      "description": "transition.rs transition, the body of contract decide-intent (CT-001) through kernel-transition, and the decision of execute-intent (CT-031, execute-decide) and mutate-record (CT-263, decide-mutation): decide an intent against a snapshot, purely. The snapshot must be of the context's tenant (TenantMismatch, tenant:snapshot_matches_context); CreateTenant needs no tenant (TenantExists, tenant:does_not_exist), every other intent an existing one (TenantNotFound, tenant:exists) that is the context's (TenantMismatch, \"snapshot holds another tenant\"). A principal id that starts with the reserved prefix team: (the caller, the owner of a new tenant, the principal an assignment or a team membership names) is InvalidIntent, principal:id_is_not_reserved (reserved-principal). Then the intent's own function fills a fresh draft (the dispatch's CreateTenant arm cannot be reached), and finish makes the transition. The revoke-invitation intent runs revoke-invitation (ADM-1083). texts are the printed expressions and the blank-name fact (intent-texts). The invoke-operation intent is refused here (operation:decided_by_the_kernel): the hand-written kernel decides it in crates/kernel/src/operations.rs (WG-5100), and the differential lists the difference. The erase-subject and invoke-operation intents are refused here (erasure:decided_by_the_kernel, operation:decided_by_the_kernel): the hand-written kernel decides them in crates/kernel/src/erasure.rs and operations.rs, and the differential lists each difference. The write-setting intent is decided by write-setting (settings.rs).",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "state",
          "type": "state"
        },
        {
          "name": "intent",
          "type": "intent"
        },
        {
          "name": "ctx",
          "type": "context"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "transition-result",
      "errors": "rejection",
      "body": "if state.tenant-id != ctx.tenant then fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.tenant-mismatch, 'tenant:snapshot_matches_context', format('snapshot is of {}, context names {}', state.tenant-id, ctx.tenant)))) else match call reserved-principal(intent, ctx) { Some(message) => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'principal:id_is_not_reserved', message))), None => match intent { create-tenant{name, owner} => match state.tenant { None => try call create-tenant(ctx, name, owner), Some(_) => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.tenant-exists, 'tenant:does_not_exist', 'the tenant already exists'))) }, _ => match state.tenant { None => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.tenant-not-found, 'tenant:exists', 'no such tenant'))), Some(t) => if t.id != ctx.tenant then fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.tenant-mismatch, 'tenant:snapshot_matches_context', 'snapshot holds another tenant'))) else let d = draft{tenant: t, ctx, coverage: state.coverage, ops: [], events: [], effects: [], evidence: [], next-record: t.next-record} in let done = match intent { create-tenant => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.tenant-exists, 'tenant:does_not_exist', 'the tenant already exists'))), change-schema{changes, expected-version, existing} => try call change-schema(d, changes, expected-version, existing), assign-role{principal: p, role} => try call change-member(d, p, role, true), assign-scoped-role{principal: p, role, object, scope: predicate} => try call decide-assign-scoped-role(d, p, role, object, predicate), revoke-scoped-role{principal: p, role, object} => try call decide-revoke-scoped-role(d, p, role, object), revoke-role{principal: p, role} => try call change-member(d, p, role, false), define-team{team, label} => try call define-team(d, team, label), assign-team-role{team, role} => try call team-role(d, team, role, true), revoke-team-role{team, role} => try call team-role(d, team, role, false), add-team-member{team, principal: p} => try call team-member(d, team, p, true), remove-team-member{team, principal: p} => try call team-member(d, team, p, false), create-invitation{invitation, address, roles} => try call create-invitation(d, invitation, address, roles), redeem-invitation{invitation} => try call redeem-invitation-intent(d, invitation), revoke-invitation{invitation} => try call revoke-invitation(d, invitation), create-record{object, fields} => try call create-record(d, object, fields), update-record{object, id, fields, expected-version} => try call update-record(d, object, id, fields, expected-version), delete-record{object, id, expected-version} => try call delete-record(d, object, id, expected-version), erase-subject => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'erasure:decided_by_the_kernel', 'an erasure of a data subject is decided by the kernel module erasure.rs, which these functions do not state yet'))), write-setting{setting, level, team, value, expected-revision: expected} => try call write-setting(d, setting, level, team, value, expected), invoke-operation => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'operation:decided_by_the_kernel', 'an invocation of a tenant operation is decided by the kernel module operations.rs, which these functions do not state yet'))), post-ledger{postings} => let checked = try call ledger-intent-decision(d, postings) in fail(rejection.rejected(call ledger-refused(checked, error-kind.invalid-intent, 'ledger:decided_by_the_ledger_module', 'a posting whose first request passes the checks made before its account is read is decided by the kernel ledger module (the account is named by a uuid derived from a SHA-256, which these functions cannot compute: WG-5257, WG-5258)'))), post-ledger-transaction{transaction} => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'ledger:decided_by_the_ledger_module', 'a ledger transaction is decided by the kernel ledger module, which these functions do not mirror'))), expire-ledger => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'ledger:decided_by_the_ledger_module', 'the expiry of credits is decided by the kernel ledger module, which these functions do not mirror'))), expire-records => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'retention:decided_by_the_kernel', 'a deletion of the records past their retention is decided by the kernel module retention.rs, which these functions do not state yet'))), refresh-computed => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'computed:decided_by_the_kernel', 'a refresh of computed fields is decided by the kernel module computed.rs, which these functions do not state yet'))), file-hold => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'hold:decided_by_the_kernel', 'the filing of a held operation is decided by the kernel module holds.rs, which these functions do not state yet'))), decide-hold => fail(rejection.rejected(call refuse(error-kind.invalid-intent, 'hold:decided_by_the_kernel', 'the decision on a held operation is decided by the kernel module holds.rs, which these functions do not state yet'))) } in try call after-decision(t, ctx, call finish(done.draft, done.output)) } } }",      "examples": [        {
