    {
      "id": "self-action-problem",
      "description": "definitions.rs operation_problems (D-8405, ADM-1613): the problem of the field that names the person an operation's subject is about: a field the object type does not declare, or one that does not hold text. The refusal of an invocation by that person (operations.rs stage_subject, SelfAction) is decided with the invocation, which these functions do not state (difference 15); self-action-refused states the comparison it makes.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        },
        {
          "name": "at",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "sub",
          "type": "tenant-operation-subject"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<string>",
      "body": "match sub.self-action { None => [], Some(person) => match get(match get(schema.objects, sub.object) { Some(o) => o.fields, None => {} }, person) { None => [format('{}: self-action field {} is not a field of {}', at, person, sub.object)], Some(f) => match f.ty { str => [], _ => [format('{}: self-action field {} of {} is not text', at, person, sub.object)] } } }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "operation approve",
            "sub": {
              "object": "note",
              "input": "note",
              "self-action": "slug"
            }
          },
          "result": []
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "operation approve",
            "sub": {
              "object": "note",
              "input": "note",
              "self-action": "rank"
            }
          },
          "result": [
            "operation approve: self-action field rank of note is not text"
          ]
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "operation approve",
            "sub": {
              "object": "note",
              "input": "note",
              "self-action": "owner"
            }
          },
          "result": [
            "operation approve: self-action field owner is not a field of note"
          ]
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "operation approve",
            "sub": {
              "object": "note",
              "input": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "self-action-refused",
      "description": "operations.rs stage_subject (D-8405, ADM-1613): whether an invocation is refused with self-action: the subject record holds, in the field the operation names, the id of the principal that invokes it, whatever roles the principal holds. A principal that is not a person is never refused.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "principal",
          "type": "principal"
        },
        {
          "name": "record",
          "type": "record"
        },
        {
          "name": "field",
          "type": "field-id"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "bool",
      "body": "match principal { user(actor) => match get(record.fields, field) { Some(v) => match v { str(who) => who == actor, _ => false }, None => false }, _ => false }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:ann"
            },
            "record": {
              "id": 1,
              "object": "note",
              "version": 1,
              "created-by": "alpha:ann",
              "created-at": 1,
              "updated-at": 1,
              "fields": {
                "slug": {
                  "str": "alpha:ann"
                }
              }
            },
            "field": "slug"
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:bob"
            },
            "record": {
              "id": 1,
              "object": "note",
              "version": 1,
              "created-by": "alpha:ann",
              "created-at": 1,
              "updated-at": 1,
              "fields": {
                "slug": {
                  "str": "alpha:ann"
                }
              }
            },
            "field": "slug"
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "principal": "system",
            "record": {
              "id": 1,
              "object": "note",
              "version": 1,
              "created-by": "alpha:ann",
              "created-at": 1,
              "updated-at": 1,
              "fields": {
                "slug": {
                  "str": "alpha:ann"
                }
              }
            },
            "field": "slug"
          },
          "result": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scoped-role-problems",
      "description": "scoped.rs problems (D-8403): more than 10000 assignments, then each assignment in the order it was made: a role that does not exist, a role that is public or owner, a predicate that does not check (scope-problem); then each role of a principal on an object type that is assigned more than once, in the order of principal, role and object.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<string>",
      "let": [
        {
          "name": "uniq",
          "expr": "match schema.scoped-roles { None => [], Some(held) => fold(a in sortBy(a in held, format('{} {} {}', a.principal, a.role, a.object)), acc = [], if any(x in acc, format('{} {} {}', x.principal, x.role, x.object) == format('{} {} {}', a.principal, a.role, a.object)) then acc else concat(acc, [a])) }"
        }
      ],
      "body": "match schema.scoped-roles { None => [], Some(held) => concat(concat(if length(held) > 10000 then [format('limit: {} scoped role assignments is more than the maximum of 10000', length(held))] else [], fold(a in held, ps = [], let at = format('scoped role {} of {} on {}', a.role, a.principal, a.object) in concat(concat(concat(ps, if get(schema.roles, a.role) == null then [format('{}: unknown role', at)] else []), if a.role == 'owner' || a.role == 'public' then [format('{}: the role is not narrowed by a scope', at)] else []), match call scope-predicate-problem(schema, a.object, a.scope) { Some(p) => [format('{}: {}', at, p.message)], None => [] }))), fold(a in uniq, ps = [], let n = length(filter(x in held, format('{} {} {}', x.principal, x.role, x.object) == format('{} {} {}', a.principal, a.role, a.object))) in if n > 1 then concat(ps, [format('scoped role {} of {} on {} is assigned {} times', a.role, a.principal, a.object, n)]) else ps)) }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            }
          },
          "result": []
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6",
              "with": {
                "scoped-roles": [
                  {
                    "principal": "alpha:ann",
                    "role": "editor",
                    "object": "note",
                    "scope": {
                      "cmp": {
                        "op": "eq",
                        "left": {
                          "var": {
                            "scope": "record",
                            "field": "slug"
                          }
                        },
                        "right": {
                          "lit": {
                            "str": "north"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "result": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "has-double-underscore",
      "description": "capabilities.rs is_product_form: whether a name holds the namespace separator, two underscores in a row, anywhere.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "name",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "bool",
      "body": "fold(c in chars(name), acc = '', if acc == '!' then acc else if c == '_' then (if acc == '_' then '!' else '_') else '') == '!'",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "name": "shop__tier"
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "name": "ledger-post"
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "name": "a_b_c"
          },
          "result": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "separation-problems",
      "description": "duties.rs problems (D-8482, ADM-1642): more than 200 declared separations, then each in id order: the key is not the id, the id is a platform separation's, the two capabilities are one, and per side a capability without a name or of the product form that the tenant does not declare, and a duty without a sentence.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<string>",
      "body": "match schema.separations { None => [], Some(declared) => concat(if length(keys(declared)) > 200 then [format('limit: {} separations is more than the maximum of 200', length(keys(declared)))] else [], fold(k in keys(declared), ps = [], match get(declared, k) { None => ps, Some(def) => let at = format('separation {}', k) in concat(concat(concat(concat(concat(concat(ps, if k != def.id then [format('{}: the key is not the id {}', at, def.id)] else []), if k == 'ledger-adjust-and-review' then [format('{}: the id is a separation of the platform', at)] else []), if def.left == def.right then [format('{}: it names the capability {} twice', at, def.left)] else []), call separation-side-problems(schema, at, 'left', def.left, def.left-duty)), call separation-side-problems(schema, at, 'right', def.right, def.right-duty)), []) })) }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            }
          },
          "result": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "separation-side-problems",
      "description": "duties.rs problems, one side of a separation: a capability without a name, or of the product form that the tenant does not declare, and a duty without a sentence.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        },
        {
          "name": "at",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "side",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "capability",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "duty",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<string>",
      "body": "concat(if trim(capability) == '' then [format('{}: the {} capability needs a name', at, side)] else if call has-double-underscore(capability) && get(call capabilities-of(schema), capability) == null then [format('{}: capability {} is neither a platform capability nor declared in the tenant', at, capability)] else [], if trim(duty) == '' then [format('{}: the {} duty needs a sentence', at, side)] else [])",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "separation a",
            "side": "left",
            "capability": "ledger-post",
            "duty": "posts"
          },
          "result": []
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "separation a",
            "side": "right",
            "capability": " ",
            "duty": " "
          },
          "result": [
            "separation a: the right capability needs a name",
            "separation a: the right duty needs a sentence"
          ]
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-6"
            },
            "at": "separation a",
            "side": "left",
            "capability": "shop__tier",
            "duty": "posts"
          },
          "result": [
            "separation a: capability shop__tier is neither a platform capability nor declared in the tenant"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "teams-of",
      "description": "TenantSchema::all_teams as a map: the teams of a schema by id, none when it holds no table of teams.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "map<team-id, team-def>",
      "body": "match schema.teams { Some(ts) => ts, None => {} }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-19"
            }
          },
          "result": {
            "desk": {
              "id": "desk",
              "label": "Desk",
              "members": [
                "alpha:guest"
              ],
              "roles": [
                "editor"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-8"
            }
          },
          "result": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "invitations-of",
      "description": "TenantSchema::all_invitations as a map: the invitations of a schema by id, none when it holds no table of invitations.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "map<invitation-id, invitation-def>",
      "body": "match schema.invitations { Some(xs) => xs, None => {} }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-8",
              "with": {
                "invitations": {
                  "inv-1": {
                    "id": "inv-1",
                    "address": "guest@example.org",
                    "roles": [
                      "editor"
                    ],
                    "created-by": "alpha:owner",
                    "redeemed-by": null
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "result": {
            "inv-1": {
              "id": "inv-1",
              "address": "guest@example.org",
              "roles": [
                "editor"
              ],
              "created-by": "alpha:owner",
              "redeemed-by": null
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-8"
            }
          },
          "result": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assigned-roles",
      "description": "rules.rs assigned_roles: the roles a person holds through the table of members and the teams of a schema: those assigned to it directly and those of each team it belongs to, and no other.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "members",
          "type": "map<principal-id, set<role-id>>"
        },
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        },
        {
          "name": "id",
          "type": "principal-id"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "set<role-id>",
      "let": [
        {
          "name": "direct",
          "expr": "match get(members, id) { Some(rs) => rs, None => [] }"
        }
      ],
      "body": "call set-of(fold(t in values(call teams-of(schema)), acc = direct, if any(m in t.members, m == id) then concat(acc, t.roles) else acc))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "A member of a team holds its roles beside its own.",
          "args": {
            "members": {
              "alpha:guest": [
                "writer"
              ]
            },
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-19"
            },
            "id": "alpha:guest"
          },
          "result": [
            "editor",
            "writer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "Someone in no team holds only what is assigned to it.",
          "args": {
            "members": {
              "alpha:editor": [
                "editor"
              ],
              "alpha:owner": [
                "owner"
              ],
              "alpha:writer1": [
                "writer"
              ],
              "alpha:writer2": [
                "writer"
              ]
            },
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-19"
            },
            "id": "alpha:writer1"
          },
          "result": [
            "writer"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grant-key",
      "description": "The order of strata_kernel::Grant as a text key: a capability before an object grant, capabilities by name, object grants by object type and then by ObjectAction in its declared order.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "g",
          "type": "grant"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "string",
      "body": "match g { capability(name) => '0' + name, object{object, action} => format('1{} {}', object, match action { read => '0', create => '1', update => '2', delete => '3' }) }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "capability": "content-write"
            }
          },
          "result": "0content-write"
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "update"
              }
            }
          },
          "result": "1note 2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grant-set",
      "description": "A BTreeSet<Grant> as the body language holds it: the grants in the kernel order (grant-key), each once.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "items",
          "type": "list<grant>"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<grant>",
      "body": "fold(g in sortBy(g in items, call grant-key(g)), acc = [], if any(x in acc, x == g) then acc else concat(acc, [g]))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "items": [
              {
                "object": {
                  "object": "note",
                  "action": "update"
                }
              },
              {
                "capability": "content-write"
              },
              {
                "object": {
                  "object": "note",
                  "action": "read"
                }
              },
              {
                "capability": "content-write"
              }
            ]
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "capability": "content-write"
            },
            {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "update"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grants-of",
      "description": "schema.rs TenantSchemaExt::grants_of: every grant of a role, from its permissions (PermissionExt::grants); a role without permissions grants none.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        },
        {
          "name": "role",
          "type": "role-id"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<grant>",
      "let": [
        {
          "name": "permissions",
          "expr": "match schema.role-permissions { Some(t) => match get(t, role) { Some(ps) => ps, None => [] }, None => [] }"
        }
      ],
      "body": "call grant-set(fold(p in permissions, acc = [], concat(acc, match p { capability(name) => [grant.capability(name)], object{object, actions} => map(a in actions, grant.object{object, action: a}) })))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-20"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "capability": "content-write"
            },
            {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "update"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "A role without permissions grants none.",
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-8"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "effective-permissions",
      "description": "rules.rs effective_permissions (ADM-151): the union of the grants of every role in roles-of, directly or through a team. The owner holds every permission, which may-confer decides, not this.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "tenant-state"
        },
        {
          "name": "principal",
          "type": "principal"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<grant>",
      "body": "call grant-set(fold(r in call roles-of(tenant, principal), acc = [], concat(acc, call grants-of(tenant.schema, r))))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-15",
              "with": {
                "members.alpha:writer1": [
                  "editor",
                  "writer"
                ]
              }
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            }
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "capability": "content-write"
            },
            {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "update"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grant-text",
      "description": "rules.rs describe_grant: a grant as a sentence fragment, capability <name> or <object>:<verb>.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "g",
          "type": "grant"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "string",
      "body": "match g { capability(name) => format('capability {}', name), object{object, action} => format('{}:{}', object, match action { read => 'read', create => 'create', update => 'update', delete => 'delete' }) }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "capability": "content-write"
            }
          },
          "result": "capability content-write"
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "update"
              }
            }
          },
          "result": "note:update"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "may-confer",
      "description": "rules.rs may_confer (ADM-152, ADM-1080): whether a principal may confer a role, which it may only when it holds every permission and capability the role grants, whether through its permissions or through a policy of the schema (a policy grants one power per action it names: holds-policy-power). A role that grants nothing, by permissions or policies, may be conferred, except owner, which only an owner confers. The check names the rule and the role; a refusal names what the principal lacks, the permissions first and then the policy powers. Taking a role away asks the same.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "tenant-state"
        },
        {
          "name": "principal",
          "type": "principal"
        },
        {
          "name": "role",
          "type": "role-id"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "check",
      "let": [
        {
          "name": "rule",
          "expr": "format('permission:confer:{}', role)"
        },
        {
          "name": "owner",
          "expr": "any(r in call roles-of(tenant, principal), r == 'owner')"
        },
        {
          "name": "grants",
          "expr": "call grants-of(tenant.schema, role)"
        },
        {
          "name": "held",
          "expr": "call effective-permissions(tenant, principal)"
        },
        {
          "name": "missing",
          "expr": "if owner then [] else filter(g in grants, !any(h in held, h == g))"
        },
        {
          "name": "powers",
          "expr": "fold(p in values(tenant.schema.policies), acc = [], if p.role != role then acc else concat(acc, map(a in p.actions, if call holds-policy-power(tenant, principal, a, p.resource, p.condition) then '' else format('policy {}: {} on {}', p.id, call action-debug(a), call resource-debug(p.resource)))))"
        },
        {
          "name": "lacking",
          "expr": "concat(map(g in missing, call grant-text(g)), filter(s in powers, s != ''))"
        }
      ],
      "body": "if role == 'owner' then (if owner then check{rule, passed: true, detail: 'an owner confers owner'} else check{rule, passed: false, detail: 'only an owner confers the owner role'}) else if grants == [] && powers == [] then check{rule, passed: true, detail: format('role {} grants no permission', role)} else if lacking == [] then check{rule, passed: true, detail: format('holds every permission that role {} grants', role)} else check{rule, passed: false, detail: format('lacks {} of the {} permissions that role {} grants: {}', length(lacking), length(grants) + length(powers), role, fold(s in lacking, acc = '', if acc == '' then s else acc + ', ' + s))}",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "An owner confers owner.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-14"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:owner"
            },
            "role": "owner"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:owner",
            "passed": true,
            "detail": "an owner confers owner"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "Only an owner confers owner.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-14"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:editor"
            },
            "role": "owner"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:owner",
            "passed": false,
            "detail": "only an owner confers the owner role"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A role that grants nothing has nothing to over-grant.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-14"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": true,
            "detail": "role editor grants no permission"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "An editor holds every grant of editor.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-15"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:editor"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": true,
            "detail": "holds every permission that role editor grants"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A writer lacks two of the three grants of editor.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-15"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": false,
            "detail": "lacks 2 of the 3 permissions that role editor grants: capability content-write, note:update"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "The owner holds every permission.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-15"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:owner"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": true,
            "detail": "holds every permission that role editor grants"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A role whose power is given by a policy is not a role that grants nothing: the owner holds every power it names.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-14",
              "with": {
                "schema.policies.editors_manage_notes": {
                  "id": "editors_manage_notes",
                  "role": "editor",
                  "resource": {
                    "object": "note"
                  },
                  "actions": [
                    "read",
                    "update",
                    "delete"
                  ],
                  "condition": null
                }
              }
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:owner"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": true,
            "detail": "holds every permission that role editor grants"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A principal who holds only some of the powers of the policies of a role lacks the others: writer1 may read notes but not update or delete them, so may not confer editor.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-17",
              "with": {
                "schema.policies": {
                  "editors_manage_notes": {
                    "id": "editors_manage_notes",
                    "role": "editor",
                    "resource": {
                      "object": "note"
                    },
                    "actions": [
                      "read",
                      "update",
                      "delete"
                    ],
                    "condition": null
                  },
                  "writers_read_notes": {
                    "id": "writers_read_notes",
                    "role": "writer",
                    "resource": {
                      "object": "note"
                    },
                    "actions": [
                      "read"
                    ],
                    "condition": null
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": false,
            "detail": "lacks 2 of the 3 permissions that role editor grants: policy editors_manage_notes: Update on Object(ObjectTypeId(\"note\")), policy editors_manage_notes: Delete on Object(ObjectTypeId(\"note\"))"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A permission of the principal covers a policy power: writer1 holds note:update through its role permissions and the policy of the editor role names only that.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-19",
              "with": {
                "schema.policies.editors_update": {
                  "id": "editors_update",
                  "role": "editor",
                  "resource": {
                    "object": "note"
                  },
                  "actions": [
                    "update"
                  ],
                  "condition": null
                }
              }
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "role": "editor"
          },
          "result": {
            "rule": "permission:confer:editor",
            "passed": true,
            "detail": "holds every permission that role editor grants"
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A conditional policy power is held through an unconditional policy of the principal: writer1 updates any note, so holds the conditioned update of the editor role as well.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-17",
              "with": {
                "schema.policies": {
                  "editors_update": {
                    "id": "editors_update",
