    {
      "id": "rule-missing",
      "description": "crates/kernel/src/expr.rs missing / first_missing: the first record, in the order the expression is written, that a reference the expression follows points at and the snapshot does not cover; none when every reference it can follow is covered. A reference is followed as eval follows it: from a single reference field of the scope's record; where eval could not follow it (no record in the scope, a null or non-reference value, a field that is not a single reference) there is no need. rules.rs authorize_needing asks it of a condition that failed to evaluate, so a decision never rests on a record that was merely not loaded. Structural recursion: every call of itself is on a field of a variant matched from e, or an item of a list such a field holds.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "e",
          "type": "expr"
        },
        {
          "name": "reach",
          "type": "rule-reach"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "option<need>",
      "body": "match e { through{scope: s, reference: f} => match call scope-record(reach.subject, s) { None => null, Some(r) => match get(r.fields, f) { None => null, Some(v) => match v { ref(target) => match call single-reference(reach.tenant.schema, r.object, f) { Some(object) => if call covers(reach.coverage, need.record{object, id: target}) then null else need.record{object, id: target}, None => null }, _ => null } } }, not(a) => call rule-missing(a, reach), is-null(a) => call rule-missing(a, reach), len(a) => call rule-missing(a, reach), lower(a) => call rule-missing(a, reach), is-slug(a) => call rule-missing(a, reach), text(a) => call rule-missing(a, reach), duration{amount} => call rule-missing(amount, reach), and(items) => fold(i in items, found = null, if found != null then found else call rule-missing(i, reach)), or(items) => fold(i in items, found = null, if found != null then found else call rule-missing(i, reach)), cmp{left, right} => let x = call rule-missing(left, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(right, reach), in{item, list: l} => let x = call rule-missing(item, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(l, reach), contains{haystack, needle} => let x = call rule-missing(haystack, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(needle, reach), starts-with{text: t, prefix} => let x = call rule-missing(t, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(prefix, reach), arith{left, right} => let x = call rule-missing(left, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(right, reach), ms-between{from: a, to: b} => let x = call rule-missing(a, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(b, reach), concat{left, right} => let x = call rule-missing(left, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(right, reach), if{condition: c, then: a, else: b} => let y = call rule-missing(c, reach) in if y != null then y else let x = call rule-missing(a, reach) in if x != null then x else call rule-missing(b, reach), _ => null }",
