    {
      "id": "after-decision-run",
      "description": "triggers.rs after_decision, past the gate: the state after the transition (apply-delta); when the transition changed members or the schema (authority-changed), the suspension of the automations whose definer lost authority (suspend-lost of lost-authorities); then, for each event of the transition in sequence order, the AutomationSuspended events included, and each trigger of the state after the suspension whose event matches it, in trigger id order, the effect decide-trigger gives, appended to the effects (D-7200). The hop of the decisions is the hop of the context, none being zero.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "t",
          "type": "tenant-state"
        },
        {
          "name": "ctx",
          "type": "context"
        },
        {
          "name": "result",
          "type": "transition-result"
        },
        {
          "name": "authority-changed",
          "type": "bool"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "transition-result",
      "errors": "rejection",
      "body": "let after0 = try call apply-delta(t, result.delta) in let sus = call suspend-lost(after0, ctx, result, if authority-changed then call lost-authorities(after0) else []) in let hop = match ctx.hop { Some(h) => h, None => 0 } in let effects = fold(e in sus.result.events, acc = [], concat(acc, fold(tr in values(call triggers-of(sus.after.schema)), found = [], if call trigger-matches(tr.on, e.body) then (match call decide-trigger(sus.after, ctx, hop, e, tr) { Some(f) => concat(found, [f]), None => found }) else found))) in transition-result{delta: sus.result.delta, events: sus.result.events, effects: concat(sus.result.effects, effects), evidence: sus.result.evidence, output: sus.result.output}",
      "examples": [
        {
