    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-change-needs",
      "description": "ledger.rs schema_change_needs: the needs of the ledger changes of a schema change: whether an account names a unit or a pool being removed (LDG-1549), the limit of the one account a removed account limit names (D-6554), and every limit of single accounts when an account limit is set, to count them against the ceiling (D-7881, LDG-1550).",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "changes",
          "type": "list<schema-change>"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<need>",
      "body": "fold(c in changes, acc = [], match c { remove-ledger-definition(r) => match r { unit{unit} => concat(acc, [need.ledger(ledger-need.unit-used{unit})]), pool{pool} => concat(acc, [need.ledger(ledger-need.pool-used{pool})]), limit{unit, owner, scope} => match owner { Some(o) => concat(acc, [need.ledger(ledger-need.limit{owner: o, unit, scope: match scope { Some(s) => s, None => '' }})]), None => acc } }, set-ledger-limit(l) => match l.owner { Some(o) => concat(acc, [need.ledger(ledger-need.limits)]), None => acc }, _ => acc })",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "changes": []
          },
          "result": []
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "changes": [
              {
                "remove-ledger-definition": {
                  "unit": {
                    "unit": "credits"
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "remove-ledger-definition": {
                  "pool": {
                    "pool": "promo"
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "remove-ledger-definition": {
                  "limit": {
                    "unit": "credits"
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "declare-ledger-unit": {
                  "unit": "x",
                  "description": "x"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "ledger": {
                "unit-used": {
                  "unit": "credits"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "ledger": {
                "pool-used": {
                  "pool": "promo"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "Setting the limit of one account asks for every limit of single accounts; setting the limit of a unit asks for nothing.",
          "args": {
            "changes": [
              {
                "set-ledger-limit": {
                  "unit": "credits",
                  "owner": {
                    "principal": {
                      "principal": "user:ines"
                    }
                  },
                  "cap": 100
                }
              },
              {
                "set-ledger-limit": {
                  "unit": "credits",
                  "floor": 0
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "ledger": "limits"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "Removing the limit of one account asks for that account's limit, in its scope or in none; removing the limit of a unit asks for nothing.",
          "args": {
            "changes": [
              {
                "remove-ledger-definition": {
                  "limit": {
                    "unit": "credits",
                    "owner": {
                      "principal": {
                        "principal": "user:ines"
                      }
                    },
                    "scope": "spring"
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "remove-ledger-definition": {
                  "limit": {
                    "unit": "credits",
                    "owner": {
                      "pool": {
                        "pool": "promo"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "ledger": {
                "limit": {
                  "owner": {
                    "principal": {
                      "principal": "user:ines"
                    }
                  },
                  "unit": "credits",
                  "scope": "spring"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "ledger": {
                "limit": {
                  "owner": {
                    "pool": {
                      "pool": "promo"
                    }
                  },
                  "unit": "credits",
                  "scope": ""
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-limit-step",
      "description": "ledger.rs check_limits, one change: the limit of one account that a change sets or removes (LDG-1550, D-6554, WG-5172). Account limits live in the ledger's storage and not in the schema. Setting one: the snapshot must hold the limits of single accounts (the need limits) unless an earlier change loaded them, or the change is InsufficientState naming it; one of a new account when max are held is LimitExceeded \"too-many: a tenant holds at most <max> account limits\" with the failed check ledger:too-many-limits; otherwise the limit replaces the one of its account among those held and ledger:account-limits passes with \"<n> account limit(s) after the change\". Removing one: from the limits held when an earlier change loaded them, otherwise the snapshot must hold the limit of that account (the need limit); one that is not held is InvalidSchema \"no such limit of ledger unit <unit>\" with the failed check ledger:limit-exists. The checks are written after the evidence of the walk. Any other change leaves the walk as it is.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "d",
          "type": "draft"
        },
        {
          "name": "w",
          "type": "ledger-limit-walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "c",
          "type": "schema-change"
        },
        {
          "name": "max",
          "type": "u64"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "ledger-limit-walk",
      "errors": "rejection",
      "let": [
        {
          "name": "stored-limits",
          "expr": "match d.tenant.ledger { Some(s) => match s.limits { Some(ls) => ls, None => [] }, None => [] }"
        }
      ],
      "body": "match c { set-ledger-limit(l) => match l.owner { Some(_) => let wanted = need.ledger(ledger-need.limits) in if w.held == null && !call covers(d.coverage, wanted) then fail(rejection.rejected(call insufficient(wanted))) else let text = call ledger-scope-text(l.scope) in let all = match w.held { Some(h) => h, None => filter(x in stored-limits, x.owner != null) } in if !any(x in all, call ledger-same-limit(x, l.unit, l.owner, text)) && length(all) >= max then fail(rejection.rejected(domain-error{kind: error-kind.limit-exceeded, message: format('too-many: a tenant holds at most {} account limits', max), evidence: concat(w.evidence, [check{rule: 'ledger:too-many-limits', passed: false, detail: format('too-many: a tenant holds at most {} account limits', max)}])})) else let after = concat(filter(x in all, !call ledger-same-limit(x, l.unit, l.owner, text)), [l]) in ledger-limit-walk{evidence: concat(w.evidence, [check{rule: 'ledger:account-limits', passed: true, detail: format('{} account limit(s) after the change', length(after))}]), held: after}, None => w }, remove-ledger-definition(r) => match r { limit{unit, owner, scope} => match owner { Some(o) => let text = call ledger-scope-text(scope) in match w.held { Some(h) => let kept = filter(x in h, !call ledger-same-limit(x, unit, owner, text)) in if length(kept) == length(h) then fail(rejection.rejected(domain-error{kind: error-kind.invalid-schema, message: format('no such limit of ledger unit {}', unit), evidence: concat(w.evidence, [check{rule: 'ledger:limit-exists', passed: false, detail: format('no such limit of ledger unit {}', unit)}])})) else ledger-limit-walk{evidence: w.evidence, held: kept}, None => let wanted = need.ledger(ledger-need.limit{owner: o, unit, scope: match scope { Some(q) => q, None => '' }}) in if !call covers(d.coverage, wanted) then fail(rejection.rejected(call insufficient(wanted))) else if !any(x in stored-limits, call ledger-same-limit(x, unit, owner, text)) then fail(rejection.rejected(domain-error{kind: error-kind.invalid-schema, message: format('no such limit of ledger unit {}', unit), evidence: concat(w.evidence, [check{rule: 'ledger:limit-exists', passed: false, detail: format('no such limit of ledger unit {}', unit)}])})) else w }, None => w }, _ => w }, _ => w }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "A change that is not a limit of an account leaves the walk as it is.",
          "args": {
            "d": {
              "fixture": "fx-draft-28"
            },
            "w": {
              "evidence": []
            },
            "c": {
              "declare-ledger-unit": {
                "unit": "x",
                "description": "x"
              }
            },
            "max": 3
          },
          "result": {
            "evidence": []
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "The limit of a unit is not one of an account.",
          "args": {
            "d": {
              "fixture": "fx-draft-28"
            },
            "w": {
              "evidence": []
            },
            "c": {
              "set-ledger-limit": {
                "unit": "credits",
                "floor": 0
              }
            },
            "max": 3
          },
          "result": {
            "evidence": []
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "The first limit of an account loads the limits the tenant holds, and counts the one set after them.",
          "args": {
            "d": {
              "fixture": "fx-draft-28",
              "with": {
                "tenant.ledger": {
                  "accounts": {},
                  "entries": {},
                  "limits": [
                    {
                      "unit": "credits",
                      "owner": {
                        "principal": {
                          "principal": "alpha:ed"
                        }
                      },
                      "scope": "promo",
                      "cap": 5
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "w": {
              "evidence": []
            },
            "c": {
              "set-ledger-limit": {
                "unit": "credits",
                "owner": {
                  "principal": {
                    "principal": "alpha:ed"
                  }
                },
                "cap": 9
              }
            },
            "max": 3
          },
          "result": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "rule": "ledger:account-limits",
                "passed": true,
                "detail": "2 account limit(s) after the change"
              }
            ],
            "held": [
              {
                "unit": "credits",
                "owner": {
                  "principal": {
                    "principal": "alpha:ed"
                  }
                },
                "cap": 5,
                "scope": "promo"
              },
              {
                "unit": "credits",
                "owner": {
                  "principal": {
                    "principal": "alpha:ed"
                  }
                },
                "cap": 9
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "description": "A limit of the same account replaces it, and counts once; the limits held so far are not loaded again, so no need is checked.",
          "args": {
